			<div class="content" id="post-content-2498743">
									

<p>This feels more like an anomalous location than an SCP, since it doesn't actually do anything except for spooking people and killing plants. Addendum 2 hints at something bigger, but I wish it was explored more, maybe the Foundation actually discovering/triggering something while poking around in the center.</p>
<p>One other question on my mind is, if it kills plants in the area, does long-term exposure do anything to humans or animals, aside from stress and whatnot?</p>
<p>Edit: And it seems you expanded on Addendum 2 while I was writing this. I feel it could still use more details to it, but now I'm getting a vague &quot;punishment for SCP-2392-A&quot; vibe, which I like.</p>

