			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2498784">
									

<p>What's the story with the missing woman? You don't have to spell it out, but if it's going to be presented as the reason for the haunting, we should know something about it.</p>
<p>I don't think we need the first addendum. The sense of dread is established. We'd need to see something new there.</p>
<p>You could introduce the crying earlier, perhaps? Reveal something known about the location (like the missing person), and finish with revealing the face, who says something that twists the situation further. Something like that.</p>
<p>Ramp up the tension with the events, and end it with us positive that we've only scratched the surface.</p>

